  "Question": "Every step in a geometric proof must have a justification. Which of the following cannot serve as a justification for reasoning?",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "Given conditions",
    "B": "Definitions and theorems that have been learned",
    "C": "Figures look equal",
    "D": "Previously proved conclusions"
  },
  "Correct Answer": "C",
  "Accepted Answers": [],
  "Unordered Answers": false,
  "Solution": "A justification must be a given condition, a definition, an axiom, a theorem, or a previously proved conclusion. Merely “looking equal” in a diagram cannot serve as a justification.",
